  "dom_id": "step-q78571",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Consider a matrix equation $A\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $2\\times 2$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\,x & ={B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {A}^{-1}A\\,x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{2}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & ={A}^{-1}{B}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
